\title{Negation}
\date{2025-12-16T01:49:43Z}
\tag{discrete}
\taxon{Definition}

\import{discrete-macros}

\p{If #{P} is any [proposition](002P), the \em{negation} of #{P} is
written #{\neg P} (or sometimes #{\overline{P}})
and read as "not #{P}" or "It is not the case that #{P}."  #{\neg P}
is true whenever #{P} is false, and vice versa.}
